  "Question": "Harry and Terry are each told to calculate \\(8-(2+5).\\) Harry gets the correct answer. Terry ignores the parentheses and calculates \\(8-2+5.\\) If Harry’s answer is \\(H\\) and Terry’s answer is \\(T,\\) what is \\(H-T?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( -10 \\)",
    "B": "\\( -6 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 0 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 6 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 10 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Harry evaluates the parentheses first, so\n\\[\nH=8-(2+5)=8-7=1.\n\\]\nIn Terry's expression, addition and subtraction have the same priority, so he works from left to right:\n\\[\nT=8-2+5=6+5=11.\n\\]\nTherefore\n\\[\nH-T=1-11=\\boxed{-10},\n\\]\nwhich is choice A.",
